\"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"75a100629cff1e699a8cd7aeb25f493c95069daee85a9c8d1f90e9457e1d92e6","event_uuid":"594974b0-0f89-47ba-a01e-5f6b8c88afa3","position":{"commit_sha":"b6d5b2df396c549fa140793820b213371840138b","position":"1786167514067416001-594974b0-0f89-47ba-a01e-5f6b8c88afa3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Addressed plan-review BLOCK (single-turn verifier can't do a real present-state check): the on-target veto is now COHORT-RESTRICTED to CODEBASE_GROUNDED (E4/G1G2/A1/G6), mirroring asserted_capability_confirmed — enforced deterministically in orchestrator.pass3_over_findings (_restrict_on_target_veto_to_grounded forces the answer to na for non-grounded findings) AND documented in both verifier prompts. Added test_pass3_on_target_veto_restricted_to_grounded_cohort proving a tool-less non-grounded yes does NOT fire the veto while a grounded yes does.","timestamp":1786150294792800001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[operator-attested] make lint and make typecheck both pass. Verified locally in worktree ../on-target-veto (env PATH=$PWD/.venv/bin) — 'make lint' exit 0 ('All checks passed!' + ruff format --check 'all files already formatted'); 'make typecheck' exit 0 ('mypy src/rebar: Success: no issues found in 438 source files'). Also confirmed green by CI on Gerrit change 1534 patchset 3 (GitHub Actions run 31240974614): job 'build-and-test / lint + type-check' passed on all matrices, overall run conclusion=success, Verified+1.","timestamp":1786167514067416001}],"created_at":1786148871077344001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"085000de-1a2c-4fce-a960-0347858e1197","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0973-9b0a-39d4-407c"},{"link_uuid":"9aa0af04-114f-4db2-a207-7c48d4984110","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"191c-ad3c-fae1-4357"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe plan-review gate re-reviews a ticket's plan on entry into `in_progress`, including\nEXECUTION-phase re-reviews (a claimed ticket re-reviewed before close). At execution time a\nPass-1 finder can flag a plan-vs-code discrepancy that is actually the *expected* result of the\nplan's own directed work already having been done: the plan directs \"remove X\", the agent\nremoved X, and the re-review flags \"the plan references X but no symbol X exists\". During a\nPLANNING review that is a legitimate true positive; during an EXECUTION review it is a false\npositive that can block a correct, completed ticket from closing. Pass-2 has no way to drop it.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a single-answer Pass-2 VETO, mirroring the existing a8e5 absence-refuted veto, that drops\nsuch a finding only during an execution-phase review. A new plan-review-only binary sub-answer\n`current_state_satisfies_plan_goal` (na-default, OUTSIDE `GRADED_BINARY` so it never affects\nvalidity arithmetic) is set by the verifier via a present-state check: does the code AS IT IS\nNOW already satisfy the plan's directed end state? `pass3_decide` drops the finding\n(`reason=\"veto:plan-goal-satisfied\"`) only when a keyword-only `execution_review` flag is True\nAND the answer is a definite `yes`. The `execution_review` phase signal ALREADY flows from\n`decide_ops` into `orchestrator.pass3_over_findings`; this change adds the kernel-level\n`execution_review` kwarg (on `pass3_decide` and `review_kernel.pass3_over_findings`) and forwards\nthe existing orchestrator flag into that kernel call. The kwarg defaults False, so planning\nreviews and every code-review call are byte-unchanged.\n\nBecause a definite `yes` is a PRESENT-STATE code check that only the code-grounded verifier can\nactually perform, the veto is COHORT-RESTRICTED to `registry.CODEBASE_GROUNDED` — the set\n`{E4, G1G2, A1, G6, asserted-capability}`. This is analogous in intent to the\n`asserted_capability_confirmed` cohort restriction (a code-grounded gate), though it uses a\nDIFFERENT cohort set (`asserted_capability_confirmed`'s cohort is G6/E4/T3, not CODEBASE_GROUNDED).\nIt is enforced deterministically in the plan-review wrapper\n(`_restrict_on_target_veto_to_grounded` forces the answer to `na` for any finding outside the\ncohort before delegating to the kernel), not only by prompt, so a tool-less single-turn\nverification can never fire the veto.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify_models.py` — add the na-default plan-review-only binary.\n- `src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py` — add the `execution_review` kwarg to `pass3_decide` +\n  `pass3_over_findings`; add the veto branch.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py` — forward `execution_review` into the kernel call\n  and enforce the code-grounded cohort restriction (`_restrict_on_target_veto_to_grounded`).\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier.md`,\n  `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier_agentic.md` — document the sub-answer + cohort.\n- `tests/unit/test_review_kernel.py`, `tests/unit/test_plan_review.py` — tests.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: `execution_review=True` + code-grounded finding + `yes` at full validity/impact\n  ⇒ dropped with `reason=\"veto:plan-goal-satisfied\"`.\n- Edge (planning preserved): same finding with `execution_review=False` ⇒ NOT dropped.\n- Edge (definite-yes only): `no`/`insufficient`/`na`/absent under execution ⇒ NOT dropped.\n- Edge (cohort restriction): a finding whose criteria are NOT in `registry.CODEBASE_GROUNDED`\n  with `yes` under execution ⇒ NOT dropped (the wrapper forces it to `na`); a grounded finding\n  with the same answer ⇒ dropped.\n- Contract: the plan-review verification model carries the field, it is na-default, and it is\n  absent from `GRADED_BINARY` and from the base/code-review models.\n- RED/GREEN verified against the source diff; the decide veto branch is mutation-tested.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A code-grounded Pass-2 finding with `current_state_satisfies_plan_goal=\"yes\"` is dropped\n  with `reason=\"veto:plan-goal-satisfied\"` when `pass3_decide` runs with `execution_review=True`,\n  even at validity 1.0 and impact 1.0.\n- [x] The same finding is NOT dropped when `execution_review=False` (planning-phase true\n  positive preserved).\n- [x] Under `execution_review=True`, answers `no`, `insufficient`, `na`, and an absent key do\n  NOT drop the finding.\n- [x] Under `execution_review=True`, a finding whose criteria are NOT in\n  `registry.CODEBASE_GROUNDED` is NOT dropped even when its answer is `yes` (cohort restriction\n  enforced in `orchestrator.pass3_over_findings`), while a grounded finding IS dropped.\n- [x] `current_state_satisfies_plan_goal` is present on the plan-review verification model,\n  defaults to `\"na\"`, and is NOT a member of `GRADED_BINARY`; the base and code-review models do\n  not carry it.\n- [x] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass. [operator-attested]","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify_models.py","reason":"add na-default plan-review-only binary current_state_satisfies_plan_goal"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py","reason":"add execution_review kwarg + on-target veto branch to pass3_decide/pass3_over_findings"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py","reason":"thread execution_review into the kernel pass3 call"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier.md","reason":"document the new sub-answer"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier_agentic.md","reason":"document the new sub-answer"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_kernel.py","reason":"kernel veto + contract tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review.py","reason":"orchestrator threading test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0973-9b0a-39d4-407c"],["relates_to","191c-ad3c-fae1-4357"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5a1ceb39-a350-4af9-9710-aa5332e28d04","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c46b-a2e8-25e8-4059","ticket_type":"task","title":"Execution-phase Pass-2 on-target veto for completed-work false positives","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5cee22f8-a922-4913-b1df-b7d390797426","8fc2892b-772a-43ad-b169-b316f208c1a2","3c6ed748-a57d-4920-b7eb-a8530bfe13e2","df216c2c-65fe-48d8-8386-225d8e22fb39","4a15929d-32e6-43a3-906f-7a85fe09921e","2b2d46b5-f4df-4adc-83dc-b45fa5b52d75","5a1ceb39-a350-4af9-9710-aa5332e28d04","8b0694a7-47df-47f5-ac0b-5c43d5d5a78e","085000de-1a2c-4fce-a960-0347858e1197","9aa0af04-114f-4db2-a207-7c48d4984110","defc8f45-689a-4582-91a5-cfd13f6988c2","09aa6bf1-d5d3-4cb3-85c5-6bcb8d75c49b","594974b0-0f89-47ba-a01e-5f6b8c88afa3"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786167514067416002,"uuid":"1f918654-a09a-405c-8504-4dcd282ece4b"}